    "title": "Florida's top Fourth of July searches are extremely on-brand - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Yacob Reyes ,\n9 hours ago\nThis Fourth of July, Floridians are looking for pool parties, patriotic bikinis and tips on decorating golf carts.\nHere's a look at our top Google searches. 🏖️ We're all in need of a break : Tampa Bay is leading the state in searches for \"Independence Day\" and \"beach,\" and no U.S. metro has searched \" July 4th pool party \" more over the past month.\nSarasota County's Siesta Beach is the state's top-trending beach search tied to Independence Day over the past month. So, if that's where you're headed, brace for traffic. 💁‍♀️ Serving looks : The Sunshine State is searching for Independence Day \"outfits\" and \"decorations\" over four times as often as \"recipes.\"\n\"How to decorate a golf cart for 4th of July Parade\" is the top trending Independence Day \"how to\" over the past month in Florida. And this isn't a phase: Since 2004, the Ft. Myers-Naples metro area has led the nation in searches for \" golf cart decorations .\" 👙 Poolside patriotism: Our top \"red, white and blue\" search is for... bikinis.\n1",
    "summary": "This Fourth of July, Floridians are looking for pool parties, patriotic bikinis and tips on decorating golf carts. 💁‍♀️ Serving looks : The Sunshine State is searching for Independence Day \"outfits\" and \"decorations\" over four times as often as \"recipes.\" \"How to decorate a golf cart for 4th of July Parade\" is the top trending Independence Day \"how to\" over the past month in Florida. And this isn't a phase: Since 2004, the Ft. Myers-Naples metro area has led the nation in searches for \" golf cart decorations .\"",
